{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating the robot's action execution from its perception of obstacles. The specification enforces safe exploration with a strong bias toward forward progress, always turning right (clockwise) for recovery, and never enabling forward motion when any obstacle is detected. Recovery states only allow rotate_clockwise, and the supervisor returns to forward progress as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model robot's motion and perception as a single plant automaton with explicit states for clear, obstacle-front, obstacle-left, and obstacle-right.",
    "Specification automaton enforces: (1) move_forward only in clear state, (2) rotate_clockwise as the only recovery action in any obstacle state, (3) immediate return to forward progress when path_clear is observed, (4) no oscillation or unsafe transitions."
  ],
